[{:db/id "q-71209/selection/1ed0aae2effe4214754fc94c79ac0ac4cf49c93d4b7e8bd425ec71e74c17c2db" :answer/id #uuid "3bae643e-1bdc-571d-8105-14b6d1ce452a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=-2 \\\\ z=2y-5\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71209/selection/ad59d8c2189187b14462bd3b3ea4be2aaefffc349c32d6b97d103d78e42d1d24" :answer/id #uuid "5d5ba7d4-7ac0-5ba1-8b74-d7d276bde3b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=-2 \\\\ z=6y-3\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71209/selection/79459c18d6671d4f5ad82f627c2b215f201250c1603a888ed0b2e0ae1b85f980" :answer/id #uuid "958b90a8-8432-5cde-bc5e-b3fbfe24ec0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=-2 \\\\ z=2y-3\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71209/selection/90a60a155e7bd12748fdb74d38149f247028e211bde422a31a9f02561406514e" :answer/id #uuid "40768e28-22e9-5d4d-b1c9-3f1dd77a9b27" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=-2 \\\\ z=4y-3\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71209/selection/412fc2e348bd6333cf2a0934328f797fd5a55958c19a8cace7c5aea18237b32a" :answer/id #uuid "34cb866c-8fd8-5e81-a193-16af194c6d6f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=-2 \\\\ z=4y-5\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71209/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f9e8ca98-bb38-506c-8b43-32cc7b1fb8f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71209/selection/79459c18d6671d4f5ad82f627c2b215f201250c1603a888ed0b2e0ae1b85f980" :answer-field/choices ["q-71209/selection/1ed0aae2effe4214754fc94c79ac0ac4cf49c93d4b7e8bd425ec71e74c17c2db" "q-71209/selection/ad59d8c2189187b14462bd3b3ea4be2aaefffc349c32d6b97d103d78e42d1d24" "q-71209/selection/79459c18d6671d4f5ad82f627c2b215f201250c1603a888ed0b2e0ae1b85f980" "q-71209/selection/90a60a155e7bd12748fdb74d38149f247028e211bde422a31a9f02561406514e" "q-71209/selection/412fc2e348bd6333cf2a0934328f797fd5a55958c19a8cace7c5aea18237b32a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71209" :question/id #uuid "5ac15352-1fbf-549f-af42-188c0083e8a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-71209" :question/problem "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $S,$ defined by $z=f(x,y),$ with the plane $x=-2.$ Given that the point $P(-2,2,1)$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{y}={x}^{2}y+2x-y$, find the equations of the tangent line to $C$ at $P.$" :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $x=-2.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $P(-2,2,1)$ will be given by the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂y}{|}_{(-2,2)}.$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂y}$ at $(-2,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(-2,2) & =(-2)^{2}(2)+2(-2)-(2) \\\\  & =8-4-2 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-z{|}_{(-2,2)} & =\\frac{∂z}{∂y}{|}_{(-2,2)}(y-2) \\\\ z-1 & =2(y-2) \\\\ z & =2y-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(-2,2,1)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-2 \\\\ z=2y-3\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-71209/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c5685f7-71b2-58ae-8c61-f555b355d92f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71209"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71234/selection/267820830c622b393ffe4382df8255031f5f4d701cb967a984e21b780bd55b59" :answer/id #uuid "8bf5a94b-3053-5a2d-9be2-e8941d23fa72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,0,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71234/selection/546883b9441c5fb3a054379dab9c65355fde2da3d83c5d3f7f0727159514b942" :answer/id #uuid "486d9ebb-2f5f-59ee-aac1-feb69066749a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,-2,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71234/selection/fd817c8ef470b93767cdf27fb758bbdfa5bdf85b64eec97a4192227eefe74931" :answer/id #uuid "1a8ed7fe-a12e-594f-a108-0929ce3c6797" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,1,-2⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71234/selection/d6c5e7ecb1b51f321dac2b18ba47bd9e77ffb62ebc1bbba6cd9b744ee4b26782" :answer/id #uuid "d1771ec2-806f-56e1-8fc2-f90eb286008a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,2,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71234/selection/b55fab1eb102a5d57c0a5a2e0c55108292008db52428694c418a63484d580176" :answer/id #uuid "b84f05f1-2f47-5379-ab0c-8f290e0b0f70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,1,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71234/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "326dc4d2-50e3-5873-b080-f56fff5c5e6c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71234/selection/d6c5e7ecb1b51f321dac2b18ba47bd9e77ffb62ebc1bbba6cd9b744ee4b26782" :answer-field/choices ["q-71234/selection/267820830c622b393ffe4382df8255031f5f4d701cb967a984e21b780bd55b59" "q-71234/selection/546883b9441c5fb3a054379dab9c65355fde2da3d83c5d3f7f0727159514b942" "q-71234/selection/fd817c8ef470b93767cdf27fb758bbdfa5bdf85b64eec97a4192227eefe74931" "q-71234/selection/d6c5e7ecb1b51f321dac2b18ba47bd9e77ffb62ebc1bbba6cd9b744ee4b26782" "q-71234/selection/b55fab1eb102a5d57c0a5a2e0c55108292008db52428694c418a63484d580176"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71234" :question/id #uuid "7e47a1d1-b7ad-556f-b8e2-ccf1072e819b" :question/math-academy-id "q-71234" :question/problem "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $S,$ defined by $z=f(x,y),$ with the plane $x=-1.$ Given that the point $P(-1,0,\\frac{1}{2})$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{y}=\\frac{x(y-x)}{2x(y+1)}$, which of the following gives a tangent vector to $C$ at $P?$" :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface with the plane $x=-1.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve $C$ at the point $P$ will be given by the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(-1,0).$ \n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ at $(-1,0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(-1,0) & =\\frac{(-1)(0-(-1))}{2(-1)(0+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1}{-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-f(-1,0) & ={f}_{y}(-1,0)(y-0) \\\\ z-\\frac{1}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}y \\\\ z & =\\frac{1}{2}y+\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(-1,0,\\frac{1}{2})$ can be given as the intersection of two planes:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-1 \\\\ z=\\frac{1}{2}y+\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $x=-1,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,0,0⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $z=\\frac{1}{2}y+\\frac{1}{2}$ (or $y-2z+1=0$), a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨0,1,-2⟩.$\n\nFinally, to find a direction vector for the tangent line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,0,0⟩\\times ⟨0,1,-2⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =2\\,j+k \\\\  & =⟨0,2,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a tangent vector to $C$ at $P$ is $⟨0,2,1⟩.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-71234/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0325887-ce25-5d6f-bf27-d85541e1dbe0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71234"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-132585/selection/6a2248e6f4491d7909b2e33d06c08ce9f16dbb12c7cc1ba746430f25c418ec76" :answer/id #uuid "4d0665e3-460a-5613-89ab-f2af8f9e7b72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y=-2 \\\\ z=-2x+15\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132585/selection/ddd0f6befe3c083d57286d3bbc4874e0db015d2bd7189fdd593559bba5540fc2" :answer/id #uuid "2303b7a0-e6f0-5da2-8c5b-dc52f9f676e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y=-2 \\\\ z=2x+9\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132585/selection/f18cab16e3af008dcbacb36e21a25b634ce831d59a58b82f463c9b01fe70465c" :answer/id #uuid "c2311db1-071e-5ef9-8c11-f7899b0d9ebd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y=-2 \\\\ z=2x+21\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132585/selection/b439284a018f162a985a6df7097c700a4091e1daeb9bdf8de3dc185ee3962a15" :answer/id #uuid "cc7f8de1-4641-5d8b-b25c-5793b8a73f8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y=-2 \\\\ z=-4x+9\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132585/selection/10f07a243b6232ea507f28b7dc2604b7d622b7f7d88d8b733246fa33a2ae8c5a" :answer/id #uuid "6733e913-504e-5778-8c06-ca47d4373929" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y=-2 \\\\ z=-4x+21\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132585/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bee217ad-b2d9-5169-98b0-c475e414c6ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-132585/selection/10f07a243b6232ea507f28b7dc2604b7d622b7f7d88d8b733246fa33a2ae8c5a" :answer-field/choices ["q-132585/selection/6a2248e6f4491d7909b2e33d06c08ce9f16dbb12c7cc1ba746430f25c418ec76" "q-132585/selection/ddd0f6befe3c083d57286d3bbc4874e0db015d2bd7189fdd593559bba5540fc2" "q-132585/selection/f18cab16e3af008dcbacb36e21a25b634ce831d59a58b82f463c9b01fe70465c" "q-132585/selection/b439284a018f162a985a6df7097c700a4091e1daeb9bdf8de3dc185ee3962a15" "q-132585/selection/10f07a243b6232ea507f28b7dc2604b7d622b7f7d88d8b733246fa33a2ae8c5a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-132585" :question/id #uuid "25f6db5c-5ba1-51f0-8059-274ba50d3f64" :question/math-academy-id "q-132585" :question/problem "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $S,$ defined by $z=f(x,y),$ with the plane $y=-2.$ Given that the point $P(4,-2,5)$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{x}=y\\sqrt{x}$, find the equations of the tangent line to $C$ at $P.$" :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $y=-2.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $P(4,-2,5)$ will be given by the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(4,-2)}.$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}$ at $(4,-2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(4,-2)} & =(-2)\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =-2(2) \\\\  & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-z{|}_{(4,-2)} & =\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(4,-2)}(x-4) \\\\ z-5 & =-4(x-4) \\\\ z & =-4x+21\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(4,-2,5)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y=-2 \\\\ z=-4x+21\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-132585/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c5685f7-71b2-58ae-8c61-f555b355d92f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-132585"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-132593/selection/31c9bad796066c461807cc3f0a619c6ec50b49d1982df2fbb0cb5fe1744c8e3f" :answer/id #uuid "4fbfea36-5d29-5aee-b660-f9a7c359d2d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=2 \\\\ z=2y+\\pi \\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132593/selection/45fdaac8ef2a811f6665936d6ce2ed2b9bc0e23a4ef5866b26d4de87a3b35bf8" :answer/id #uuid "18e40470-6d72-53b5-a86a-938e6ef8f4ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=2 \\\\ z=2y-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132593/selection/b17e5e9b688cd8f4c3b8a1af3e94f55f7686836922ed8f036d43d2ed19cc8379" :answer/id #uuid "c41e9a55-6bf1-5031-90a2-6b4ad9e2aa6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=2 \\\\ z=4y-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132593/selection/574f2c667752f57c9d64969a38153b6c83c6d11a79d6509870a32b7aa9c834e0" :answer/id #uuid "79f9cc3e-345f-5c24-b1a0-3b48b5f6fddb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=2 \\\\ z=4y-\\pi \\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132593/selection/f036cc45ea0ddd437588b5ee1de8a7c0e293c8e758d229e5fb4cfbb5d4b95a50" :answer/id #uuid "77259452-352b-502d-afd5-e763cd888585" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=2 \\\\ z=4y\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132593/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7cb05a8e-bcc1-5318-aa7b-7ad59500d31f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-132593/selection/574f2c667752f57c9d64969a38153b6c83c6d11a79d6509870a32b7aa9c834e0" :answer-field/choices ["q-132593/selection/31c9bad796066c461807cc3f0a619c6ec50b49d1982df2fbb0cb5fe1744c8e3f" "q-132593/selection/45fdaac8ef2a811f6665936d6ce2ed2b9bc0e23a4ef5866b26d4de87a3b35bf8" "q-132593/selection/b17e5e9b688cd8f4c3b8a1af3e94f55f7686836922ed8f036d43d2ed19cc8379" "q-132593/selection/574f2c667752f57c9d64969a38153b6c83c6d11a79d6509870a32b7aa9c834e0" "q-132593/selection/f036cc45ea0ddd437588b5ee1de8a7c0e293c8e758d229e5fb4cfbb5d4b95a50"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-132593" :question/id #uuid "f33b32cc-e271-575d-84a5-5374b57e2868" :question/math-academy-id "q-132593" :question/problem "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $S,$ defined by $z=f(x,y),$ with the plane $x=2.$ Given that the point $P(2,\\frac{\\pi }{4},0)$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{y}=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)$, find the equations of the tangent line to $C$ at $P.$" :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $x=2.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $P(2,\\frac{\\pi }{4},0)$ will be given by the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂y}{|}_{(2,\\pi /4)}.$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂y}$ at $(2,\\frac{\\pi }{4}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(2,\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =4\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-z{|}_{(2,\\pi /4)} & =\\frac{∂z}{∂y}{|}_{(2,\\pi /4)}(y-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\ z-0 & =4(y-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\ z & =4y-\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(2,\\frac{\\pi }{4},0)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2 \\\\ z=4y-\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-132593/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c5685f7-71b2-58ae-8c61-f555b355d92f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-132593"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-132604/selection/67823992b9e86d4b18f53ff99b67228121b8691bd33db0ca84d8dad193a44251" :answer/id #uuid "99322434-3d73-5ed8-b308-b3368809bda5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-j+2\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132604/selection/175dd31310006722e592a33b44de7d8ca2d4ec5ac2edb14e47d442b5113371b2" :answer/id #uuid "84c0fad5-1808-54fd-a155-1192b4f21e9f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-j+k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132604/selection/ea52f7877fd2793dc99d4f0cca4177dfd6ffcca26f44b39a2749b1fceec5b9ee" :answer/id #uuid "2062157a-ebd1-5991-b6ad-331e706b1976" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "j+k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132604/selection/9f37a6e36e2bb736389474e43545e06b7f040c385477e328914fbd3c640ea102" :answer/id #uuid "825cdb80-67cc-5ec8-a729-db04bbe0c8e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2j-3k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132604/selection/7dd27701a1d3aa50ba174c2d35e6ca5e3f7b406c3065eb75d249d79365dd97bf" :answer/id #uuid "a141253e-808d-5329-9f37-b3337a4dac30" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\,j+k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132604/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8def2af8-3391-58ae-89cc-ebecfc3d6c0a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-132604/selection/175dd31310006722e592a33b44de7d8ca2d4ec5ac2edb14e47d442b5113371b2" :answer-field/choices ["q-132604/selection/67823992b9e86d4b18f53ff99b67228121b8691bd33db0ca84d8dad193a44251" "q-132604/selection/175dd31310006722e592a33b44de7d8ca2d4ec5ac2edb14e47d442b5113371b2" "q-132604/selection/ea52f7877fd2793dc99d4f0cca4177dfd6ffcca26f44b39a2749b1fceec5b9ee" "q-132604/selection/9f37a6e36e2bb736389474e43545e06b7f040c385477e328914fbd3c640ea102" "q-132604/selection/7dd27701a1d3aa50ba174c2d35e6ca5e3f7b406c3065eb75d249d79365dd97bf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-132604" :question/id #uuid "67f0915e-8edd-59e2-80b4-1117b541be88" :question/math-academy-id "q-132604" :question/problem "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $S,$ defined by $z=f(x,y),$ with the plane $x=1.$ Given that the point $P(1,0,-1)$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{y}=x{e}^{xy}-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡y$, which of the following gives a tangent vector to $C$ at $P?$" :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface with the plane $x=1.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve $C$ at the point $P$ will be given by the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(1,0).$ \n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ at $(1,0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(1,0) & =1\\cdot {e}^{1\\cdot 0}-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡0 \\\\  & =1\\cdot 1-2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-f(1,0) & ={f}_{y}(1,0)(y-0) \\\\ z-(-1) & =(-1)y \\\\ z & =-y-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(1,0,-1)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1 \\\\ z=-y-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $x=1,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,0,0⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $z=-y-1$ (or $y+z+1=0$), a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨0,1,1⟩.$\n\nFinally, to find a direction vector for the tangent line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,0,0⟩\\times ⟨0,1,1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-j+k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a tangent vector to $C$ at $P$ is $-j+k.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-132604/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0325887-ce25-5d6f-bf27-d85541e1dbe0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-132604"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
